{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Inspecting a Schedule","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/names","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Inspecting-a-Schedule"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orders.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"]]},"metadata":{"title":"ambiguities()","externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV11ambiguitiesSayAA9AmbiguityVGyF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L525"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"Systems"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The ambiguous pairs, ordered by the position of their first system and then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their second."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Such a pair runs in the order it’s written in, which is easy to change by accident. In the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"following schedule, "},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that "},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads, but nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"says which runs first:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement()","}","for ambiguity in frame.ambiguities() {","    print(frame.names[ambiguity.first], frame.names[ambiguity.second])","    \/\/ Prints \"Gravity Movement\"","}","","let ordered = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","print(ordered.ambiguities().isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Order each pair with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or mark it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when either order is right. Systems without an access"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always run alone, in the order written, and are left out. Call this method in a test to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keep a schedule free of ambiguities."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"·(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":")) for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"s"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" systems and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ordered pairs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()"]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"title":"ambiguities()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ambiguities"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentatio